f risk factors do not change); &#x02265;10, high risk.&#x000a0; <bold>Note</bold>: Of the 111 with <italic>low risk</italic> scores (3-9), 110 had a score of 5-9. They were told they are at low risk now but would be at high risk at age 45 if risk factors do not change.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Acceptability of Computerized Health Screening to Study Subjects, by Their Diabetes Risk Test Score, 2003</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" scope="col" rowspan="3" colspan="1">Survey Question</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="3" colspan="1"><bold>Total No. (%)</bold></th><th align="center" scope="col" colspan="5" rowspan="1"><bold>ADA Diabetes Risk Test Score<xref rid="T4FN1" ref-type="table-fn">a</xref></bold></th></tr><tr><th colspan="5" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Very Low RiskScore 0-2 No. (%)</bold></th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Low RiskScore 3-9<xref rid="T4FN2" ref-type="table-fn">b</xref> No. (%)</bold></th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>High RiskScore &#x02265;10 No. (%)</bold></th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Already Have Diabetes No. (%)</bold></th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>P</italic> Value<xref rid="T4FN3" ref-type="table-fn">c</xref></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" scope="col" colspan="7" rowspan="1"><bold>Is it acceptable to you to answer questions about your health on a computer?</bold></td></tr><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Not at all acceptable</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20 (8.9)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2 (4.4)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8 (8.2)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6 (9.4)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1"